2026-06-06 10:00:09,311 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] ### Answers to Investigation Questions
2026-06-06 10:00:09,311 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q1 - FTP Server Software**: Microsoft IIS FTP Service (FTPSVC2) version 8.5.0.0 on Windows Server 2012 R2 (hostname DMZ-FTP, IP 172.16.10.12, domain shieldbase.lan). HTTP service (W3SVC1) also running.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,312 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q2 - Unauthorized Accounts**: `rsydow-a` has a full interactive user profile (PowerShell cache, CREDHIST, Downloads created 2018-08-07). `rsydow-f` authenticated from external IPs (108.79.235.64, 165.227.50.129). `dblake` appears legitimate. Anonymous access was attempted but failed.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,313 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q3 - Attacker Tools/Malware**: `sub-win-x64_base-hunt_5682_3262.exe` (4,246 bytes, SHA256: 3911a78...532cb) in srl-ftp directory matches Cobalt Strike stager naming convention and has timestomped timestamps. Forensic response tools (fresponse-agent.msi, Mnemosyne.sys) also present.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,314 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q4 - FTP File Transfers**: RETR operations on `/Users/` directories from 172.16.5.26 as dblake (2018-08-07 23:30). Path reference to `Users/nfury/` found in carved email data. Data channel operations from multiple external IPs.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,316 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q5 - Lateral Movement**: WebDAV access from 172.16.5.26 to `/c$` (admin share) and `/srl-ftp` on 2018-09-07, using Windows 10 WebDAV client. Failed internal FTP auth from 172.16.7.11 as dblake.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,317 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q6 - Persistence**: GroupPolicy\Machine\Scripts\Startup directory exists (created 2018-07-16). Full persistence analysis limited by unindexed EVTX/registry.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,318 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q7 - Privilege Escalation**: Admin share (/c$) access via WebDAV implies administrator-level credentials were used from 172.16.5.26. Full assessment blocked by EVTX gap.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,319 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q8 - Event Log Tampering**: Two FTP logs selectively deleted (u_ex180805.log, u_ex180823.log) from an otherwise continuous daily sequence. Windows EVTX logs exist on disk but were not indexed for tampering analysis.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,320 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q9 - Network Connections**: External scanning from 221.151.127.218, 95.47.155.87, 138.197.213.41, 146.185.222.48, 185.255.31.2, 94.23.20.187, 196.52.43.96, 149.202.71.206. Legitimate access from Azure (40.121.0.91). Internal access from 172.16.5.26 and 172.16.7.11.
2026-06-06 10:00:09,320 INFO mulder.orchestrator.display: [dashboard] **Q10 - Timestomping**: Confirmed on `sub-win-x64_base-hunt_5682_3262.exe` — $SI Created backdated to 2013-08-22 while $FN timestamps show 2018-08-09 (actual file placement date).
